                    "fillColor": "#9ea3b0",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Loops are recorded and the engine can follow a tempo change (LooperState.tempoFollow retimes). The tempo stays editable from the readout (owner decision 4), and the note under the figure says what a change does before the hand makes it, in the warning colour, in place of 'Tap the figure to type it.'. The time signature changes only before the first take: its row dims to the disabled opacity (0.4) and its label carries the lock and 'Clear all tracks to change it'. The selected track has its own length here (8 bars against a default of 4), so the Length row's note names it: the buttons still edit the default (decision 2), and the track's own value stays a main-screen edit. The other tempo states follow the same table in the plan: no grid or no follower locks the tempo with the reason in the note, and MIDI clock locks it with 'MIDI clock sets the tempo'."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
